    <statement><p>Calculate the flux of the vector field
<m>\vec{F}(\vec{r}) = 6 \vec{r}</m>, where
<m>\vec{r} = \langle x, y, z \rangle</m>,
through a sphere of radius <m>4</m>
centered at the origin, oriented outward.</p>
<p>Flux = <fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <hint/>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>24\cdot 4\pi \cdot 4^{2}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
